    board, blue servo cases, horn discs, white printed brackets, and four outward
    legs. The screenshot is perspective-only and does not provide reliable overall
    dimensions, so all sizes, masses, and joint ranges remain placeholders. Measure
    the assembled print before treating this as a digital twin or commanding servos.

    Each leg has a coxa/yaw joint, femur/pitch joint, and tibia/knee joint.
    Existing joint and actuator names are kept for compatibility with
    control_test.py. Coordinates: X forward, Y left, Z up; lengths in metres.
